# Vulnerability details

## Impact

When calculating `liquidatorReward`, using `debtPosition.futureValue` is incorrect because `debtPosition.futureValue` represents the value in debt tokens, whereas `liquidatorReward` is in collateral token value. This discrepancy will lead to an incorrect amount of `liquidatorReward` being determined.

## Proof of Concept

`liquidatorReward` will use whichever is smaller between `assignedCollateral - debtInCollateralToken` or `Math.mulDivUp(debtPosition.futureValue, state.feeConfig.liquidationRewardPercent, PERCENT)`. However, this is incorrect because `debtPosition.futureValue` remains in debt value and is not converted to collateral value.

