# Vulnerability details

## Impact
When users want to sell existing credit by limit order, they might take more profit loss because of lots of fragmentation fees.

## Proof of Concept
When users hold one credit, and want to early exit by selling the credit. Other users can choose to become the lender via buying the existing credit. And in this case, the fragmentationFee needs to be payed by the user who sell the credit. 

The vulnerability is that the malicious user can match the credit by repeat buying one small piece of this credit. The user who sell the credit has to pay multiple times fragmentationFee, which cause large fund loss.

Considering that size protocol will be deployed in Base chain, gas fee will not be one problem for this attack.

### Poc
In below test case, Alice owns one credit with 100e6 size. Candy buys this credit by repeating buying 10e6 size credit. Alice has to pay 10 * fragmentationFee = 50e6.

